  + // Deterministic tool refusals — one definition, two readers
  + // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  + 
  + /// The opening phrase of every *deliberate* tool refusal yoyo produces.
  + ///
  + /// A refusal is deterministic: the same call will be refused the same way for
  + /// as long as the mode/cap/restriction that produced it is in place. Re-running
  + /// the turn cannot change the answer — it only spends tokens. The phrase is
  + /// written for the model and the human reading the error (it says plainly that
  + /// retrying is pointless) and doubles as the structural signal
  + /// [`is_deterministic_tool_error`] reads, so the classifier and its producers
  + /// cannot desync: every refusing wrapper builds its error through
  + /// [`deterministic_refusal`], and nothing else in the codebase writes this
  + /// phrase by hand.
